  ('reasoning', 'Blood Relations', 2, 'Pointing to a man, Neha said, "He is the only son of my grandfather''s only son." How is the man related to Neha?', array['Uncle', 'Brother', 'Cousin', 'Father'], 1, 'Neha''s grandfather''s only son is Neha''s father, and her father''s only son is her brother.', 40, 'curated_blood_relations', null, null, null),
  ('reasoning', 'Blood Relations', 2, 'A is the brother of B. B is the sister of C. C is the father of D. How is A related to D?', array['Brother', 'Father', 'Grandfather', 'Uncle'], 3, 'A, B and C are siblings. C is D''s father, so A (male) is D''s uncle.', 40, 'curated_blood_relations', null, null, null),
  ('reasoning', 'Blood Relations', 2, 'Introducing a woman, Rohit said, "Her mother is the only daughter of my mother." How is the woman related to Rohit?', array['Cousin', 'Daughter', 'Niece', 'Sister'], 2, 'The only daughter of Rohit''s mother is Rohit''s sister. The woman is his sister''s daughter, so his niece.', 40, 'curated_blood_relations', null, null, null),
  ('reasoning', 'Blood Relations', 1, 'P is the father of Q. Q is the son of R. How is R related to P?', array['Sister', 'Mother', 'Daughter', 'Wife'], 3, 'P is the father and R is the other parent of Q, so R is the mother and P''s wife.', 30, 'curated_blood_relations', null, null, null),
  ('reasoning', 'Blood Relations', 1, 'X''s mother is the sister of Y''s father. How is X related to Y?', array['Cousin', 'Nephew', 'Brother', 'Uncle'], 0, 'X''s mother and Y''s father are siblings, so X and Y are cousins.', 30, 'curated_blood_relations', null, null, null),
  ('reasoning', 'Blood Relations', 2, 'Pointing to a photo, Arun said, "She is the daughter of my grandfather''s only son." How is the girl related to Arun?', array['Niece', 'Aunt', 'Sister', 'Cousin'], 2, 'Arun''s grandfather''s only son is Arun''s father, so the girl is his father''s daughter: his sister.', 40, 'curated_blood_relations', null, null, null),
  ('reasoning', 'Blood Relations', 3, 'M is the son of N. N is the daughter of O. O is the husband of P. How is P related to M?', array['Grandmother', 'Aunt', 'Mother', 'Grandfather'], 0, 'O and P are N''s parents, and M is N''s son, so P is M''s grandmother.', 55, 'curated_blood_relations', null, null, null),
  ('reasoning', 'Blood Relations', 2, 'A''s father is B''s son. C is B''s only daughter. How is C related to A?', array['Mother', 'Grandmother', 'Sister', 'Aunt'], 3, 'C is the sister of A''s father, so C is A''s aunt.', 40, 'curated_blood_relations', null, null, null),
  ('reasoning', 'Blood Relations', 2, 'Pointing to a man, Kavya said, "His wife is my mother''s only daughter." How is the man related to Kavya?', array['Father', 'Brother-in-law', 'Husband', 'Brother'], 2, 'Kavya''s mother''s only daughter is Kavya herself, so the man is Kavya''s husband.', 40, 'curated_blood_relations', null, null, null),
  ('reasoning', 'Blood Relations', 3, 'J is the brother of K. L is the mother of J. M is the father of L. How is M related to K?', array['Father', 'Uncle', 'Grandfather', 'Brother'], 2, 'L is the mother of J and K, and M is L''s father, so M is K''s grandfather.', 55, 'curated_blood_relations', null, null, null),
  ('reasoning', 'Syllogisms', 1, 'Statements: All pens are books. All books are bags. Which conclusion follows?', array['Some bags are not books', 'All bags are pens', 'All pens are bags', 'No pen is a bag'], 2, 'Pens sit inside books, and books sit inside bags, so every pen is a bag.', 30, 'curated_syllogisms', null, null, null),
  ('reasoning', 'Syllogisms', 2, 'Statements: Some cats are dogs. All dogs are birds. Which conclusion follows?', array['All cats are birds', 'Some cats are birds', 'All birds are cats', 'No cat is a bird'], 1, 'The cats that are dogs are also birds, so some cats are birds.', 40, 'curated_syllogisms', null, null, null),
  ('reasoning', 'Syllogisms', 2, 'Statements: No apple is a mango. All mangoes are fruits. Which conclusion follows?', array['All fruits are mangoes', 'No apple is a fruit', 'Some fruits are not apples', 'Some apples are mangoes'], 2, 'Mangoes are fruits and no mango is an apple, so at least those fruits are not apples.', 40, 'curated_syllogisms', null, null, null),
  ('reasoning', 'Syllogisms', 2, 'Statements: All roses are flowers. Some flowers are red. Which conclusion definitely follows?', array['Some flowers are roses', 'All flowers are roses', 'Some roses are red', 'No rose is red'], 0, 'Since every rose is a flower, some flowers are roses. Nothing links roses to the red flowers.', 40, 'curated_syllogisms', null, null, null),
  ('reasoning', 'Syllogisms', 1, 'Statements: All doctors are graduates. No graduate is unemployed. Which conclusion follows?', array['Some doctors are unemployed', 'Some unemployed people are graduates', 'No doctor is unemployed', 'All graduates are doctors'], 2, 'Every doctor is a graduate and no graduate is unemployed, so no doctor is unemployed.', 30, 'curated_syllogisms', null, null, null),
  ('reasoning', 'Syllogisms', 2, 'Statements: Some laptops are phones. No phone is a tablet. Which conclusion follows?', array['All phones are laptops', 'No laptop is a tablet', 'Some laptops are not tablets', 'Some tablets are phones'], 2, 'The laptops that are phones cannot be tablets, so some laptops are not tablets.', 40, 'curated_syllogisms', null, null, null),
  ('reasoning', 'Analogies', 1, 'Book : Library :: Painting : ?', array['Frame', 'Artist', 'Gallery', 'Canvas'], 2, 'A library is where books are kept and shown; a gallery is where paintings are.', 30, 'curated_analogies', null, null, null),
